    "done_when": "Build items 1 and 2 of plan one-typesafe-model-picker §12; the section is the authority for them and for the done-when clauses they own. Items 3 and 4 landed at merge ff6304374 and are out of scope. Item 1: write a replay driver under the run directory that re-runs the inputs of the ten slowest picks recorded in ~/.config/reckon/crew/pick-timings.jsonl in one process. For each tail stage (snapshot_ms, state_render_ms, capability_ms), give a verdict in the manifest: load or code, with the recorded and replayed medians behind it. Item 2: cut only what is code, starting with whatever a stage reads or computes per pick that an earlier stage already holds. A stage that is slow only under load is reported, not rewritten. Run the replay driver before and after the change, and record the medians for every stage the change cut; estimate_ms is exempt. Tests go in tests/test_pick_stages_fit_the_bound.py and prove each cut keeps the pick's selection unchanged on a recorded input. Gate: that file, every tests/test_picker*.py, tests/test_pick_records_its_stage_times.py, tests/test_estimate_stage_times_the_estimate.py, tests/test_jev_sees_declared_difficulty.py, tests/test_budget_view_is_cached.py and tests/test_jev_weighs_context.py. Run the gate with the main checkout's .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 6 in the FOREGROUND, one log each for base and head under the run directory, each ending in an EXIT= line, judged by delta against the base. Command code lives in the sibling modules of reckon/cli.py; patch the module whose code reads a name. Write the evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/one-typesafe-model-picker/pick-stages-fit-the-bound.html.",
